# Label the largest files in a folder. An empty folder means the script folder.
Allow reading files
Also use "../files/folder-helpers.writ"

When run, given a folder which is a string, returning a list of string
    if the folder is nothing or the folder is equal to ""
        the folder is the script folder
    the lines are an empty list
    try to
        the files are the items in the folder, files only
    if that fails
        warn "Could not read {the folder}: {the error}"
        return the lines
    the real are the files where the length is greater than 0
    the biggest are the first 5 of the real sorted by length, largest first
    for each file in the biggest
        the size is the length of the file as an integer
        the kind is "ordinary"
        if the size is greater than 100000
            the kind is "large"
        otherwise if the size is less than 100
            the kind is "tiny"
        the described is Describe with the name of the file and the size
        the lines are the lines with "{the kind}: {the described}" added
    note "Showing {the count of the biggest} of {the count of the real}"
    say "Folder {the folder}"
    return the lines
